{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1519341-trinity-on-vtt","id":1519341,"title":"Trinity on VTT","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-08-01T08:29:20-07:00","id":1519341,"title":"Trinity on VTT","content":"I've backed every single Trinity campaign because I love the system, settings, writing, etc. However, my game group is spread across several states (we all started together in person over 40 years ago).<br /> <br /> I have been dying to play Trinity Continuum with them, with other setting sprinkled in, ever since the latest version came out.<br /> <br /> But I cannot seem to find support for any VTT. There is decent support for Vampire Masquerade (more than one VTT), so I know it is possible to support Trinity. I just can't seem to find it.<br /> <br /> If there is VTT support for any platform, I'd get it. Although my preferred VTT at this time is Fantasy Grounds, Alchemy is a close second. At this point, I'll take anything!<br /> <br /> Is there support for Trinity on any VTT?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28133-tpkurilla","name":"tpkurilla","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-01T13:00:56-07:00","id":1519353,"title":"","content":"You may wish to give <a href=\"https://foundryvtt.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Foundry VTT</a> a try, it has a very active author list and a robust builder kit. My friends and I had originally given up on Exalted as the combat was simply too much of a mess for our virtual sessions. After using Foundry for Pathfinder and SWADE for a while, someone posted a Exalted ruleset that handled combat so well it almost had us returning to it due removing most of the friction those rules have baked into the system. (We wound up not going back to Exalted, for while the automation of combat was great, its still too gimmicky for our tastes).<br /> <br /> While a search on their system library didn't turn up a TC ruleset, having used it's builder set for M&amp;M3E was admittedly a learning curve, but we managed to get a good foundation that we're steadily improving on. The community is <i>super</i> helpful and wonderfully non-toxic both on their Discord and on their Reddit page, helping us get our M&amp;M rules rolling quickly and teaching us a number of little enhancements that revolve around looking at problems from different angles. You could probably take a look at the Exalted module and tease out a approach with its builder.<br /> <br /> I've tried several different VTTs, and Foundry is hands down superior to all of them, not only is it is very robust and highly flexible, its very budget friendly. You can host the session on your own computer, or set it up to use AMZ (or any other hosting provider) with little effort, which will cost you a hosting fee, but compared to its competitors with their inhouse costs its no contest. We use AMZ S3 for hosting shared assets and otherwise run our games from our own PCs (one of my friends is a AMZ whiz and handles all that for the rest of us), two of my group are in remote areas of Canada, one is a digital nomad, and the remaining two are nearly opposite ends of the US-we rarely have loading issues or lag. Its community is highly prolific in support material with maps, tokens, etc. While admittedly the majority of community content is slated towards fantasy (d20 systems in particular) there is a growing trend of other genres taking shape thanks in good part to the growing use of AI software assisting with the community's various efforts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Reality is a matter of perception, challenging one's own or that of others is not a crime, it is a service.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12415-seeker1728","name":"Seeker1728","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12415_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-01T13:09:20-07:00","id":1519355,"title":"","content":"Thank you very much for your thoughtful advice. I may eventually have to follow it, since there seems to be a lack of interest in Trinity for VTT...which is really a shame!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28133-tpkurilla","name":"tpkurilla","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-01T14:03:49-07:00","id":1519361,"title":"","content":"<b><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1454279-character-sheet-trinity-continnum-character-sheet-project-for-roll-20\">There IS a Trinity VTT on Roll20</a></b> - only it's fan created, by <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26537-jonnes-derik\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar26537_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"26537\" data-vbnamecard=\"26537\">Jonnes.Derik</a> a.k.a. Mercury Cluster. Derik's brothers sheet have EVERYTHING that already had official premier in <b>Trinity</b> 2E - and things are prototyped for things 'in writing' in gameline. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ( Rest is not put more becuase it's Roll20 policy to greenlight sheet to officially premiered books in final PDF, not past crowdfunding only. ) I run it my TC camping for the last year at least on it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <img width=\"345\" height=\"528\" data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://i.imgur.com/TlRKxi6.png\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/TlRKxi6.png\" data-thumb-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/TlRKxi6.png\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/><br /> <br /> <img data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/9cdoi6srznhqq3s/Screenshot_5.png?raw=1\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/9cdoi6srznhqq3s/Screenshot_5.png?raw=1\" data-thumb-url=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/9cdoi6srznhqq3s/Screenshot_5.png?raw=1\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 08-02-2023, 10:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-01T14:51:10-07:00","id":1519366,"title":"","content":"@<b><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster\">wy